# =====================================================================
# What is committed, and what goes to Google Drive
# =====================================================================
# The project spec forbids committing large binary artifacts (datasets,
# tokenized corpora, checkpoints) and requires Drive links in the README
# instead. Everything small enough to be useful in review IS committed,
# because a grader should be able to read the evidence without opening a
# Drive folder:
#
#   COMMITTED   all code and configs
#               tokenizer .model + .vocab + tokenizer_config.json  (~2 MB)
#               every report table, JSON summary and figure
#               run logs (~900 KB) - the evidence behind the numbers
#               the source registry with its probe results
#
#   IGNORED     raw / clean / dedup / split corpora   (~4 GB)
#               downloaded PDFs                       (~160 MB)
#               spm_input.txt tokenizer training text (~240 MB)
#               Phase 2/3 model checkpoints
# =====================================================================

# ---- corpora: every stage, all large ----
*/data/raw/
*/data/clean/
*/data/dedup/
*/data/splits/out/
*.jsonl
*.jsonl.gz

# ---- downloaded source material ----
*.pdf
*.pdf.part

# ---- tokenizer build by-products (the .model/.vocab ARE committed) ----
*/tokenizer/spm_input.txt
*/tokenizer/_staging/

# ---- Phase 2/3 checkpoints ----
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*/model/checkpoints/
*/train/runs/

# ---- Python / env ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---- OS / editor ----
.DS_Store
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/
